\end{align*}
which only has solutions $(i, j) = (1, 1),(2, 0),(0, 2)$. Since the RHS is $9 = 3^2$, these of course can only happens if $i = 2$ and $j = 0$. Thus \begin{align*}
x &= 19^2 \cdot 89^0 i = 19^2 = 361\\
x &= 19^0 \cdot 89^2 j = 89^2 = 7921
\end{align*}
None of these numbers satisfies  $19 \lceil \frac{x}{19} \rceil − x ≥ 0$. $19 \lceil \frac{x}{19} \rceil − x = 0$ at $x = 361$. Therefore, the smallest $x$ would be $7970$. However, $19 \lceil \frac{7970}{19} \rceil − 7970 = 9$, so $7970$ is the smallest $x$ satisfying \[\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = 9 = \lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor.\] $\boxed{7970}$. [/answer]

